# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore` (not plain `.dockerignore`) on purpose:
# the build CONTEXT for this image is `docs/flows/` (the parent of this
# `viewer/` folder — the server needs both the viewer app and the sibling
# `.puml` sources in one image), but a plain `.dockerignore` is only read
# from the context root. BuildKit (the default builder since Docker 23.0)
# additionally honors a Dockerfile-adjacent `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`,
# which is exactly what this file is — kept right next to the Dockerfile
# it governs, regardless of where the build context root happens to be.

# VCS / editor / OS cruft
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp

# Node (none of this exists here today, but keep the image lean if it ever does)
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log*

# Docker meta files themselves
**/Dockerfile
**/docker-compose*.yml
**/.dockerignore

# Docs not needed at runtime (kept in source control, not in the image)
**/README.md
